From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rzxvx <rrzxznewid@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:00:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] mtd: apple-sftl: Read the 16 GB PPN layout

The iPad mini 1 ships with a 16 GB or a 64 GB Hynix PPN package. The
translation layer only registers on the 64 GB one. Add the 16 GB layout
as Cascadia measured it on a 16 GB P105 with 12H321 (iOS 8.4.1):

- two CAUs per bus, 1064 blocks of 256 pages; the FTL sees four banks in
  the order (bus 0, cau 0), (bus 1, cau 0), (bus 0, cau 1), (bus 1, cau 1),
  which is the provider's lane order;
- 1055 superblocks of 4096 slots, striped dense over the banks a VFL
  table lists for each superblock;
- the VFL in blocks 1062 and 1063 of every bank, 128 SLC pages each; the
  older bank can be erased, so page zero of either block can seed the
  member list;
- 3906250 exported and 16 hidden logical pages, the 1055-entry block,
  user sequence and read count sections of a native context;
- at least 32 range records in multiples of 16, as iOS writes the tree;
- summaries of 4 or 8 chunks, whose span can include the summary's own
  chunks ("+nb"): those sequences are accounted to the summary so the
  journal stays contiguous.

Padding records (key 0xffff0000) map nothing on either layout.

H2FMI registers the provider for both profiles. The 16 GB disk is
read-only: Cascadia's writer, checkpoint and reclamation for this layout
are not ported here.

Add a synthetic 16 GB medium to the KUnit tests: a VFL in either bank, a
native 56-record context, a closed block from before the checkpoint and a
closed block after it on three banks with a padded run and a summary that
counts its own chunks.

Ported from Cascadia (https://github.com/rzxvx/Project-Cascadia) commits
0feb4a7 ("a5: PPN NAND driver and Swiss FTL, written from the spec"),
6a67fe8 ("a5: FTL: read a context tree of any length"), 3f09b61 ("a5:
NAND: context tree length as iOS writes it; replay log of 64; rung 9
notes") and b1d85d7 ("a5: NAND spec: ladder results, long context trees,
page transmit"), files sftl.h and sftl_mount.c and
devices/a5/docs/research/p105-nand-spec.md sections 3 and 4, as of
Cascadia ad28ba4. Format findings on this package credit crystal-lized's
iPhone 5 work.

Assisted-by: LLM
